====================================================\nSECTION 10. AUDIT RESULTS (v2.0 \u2014 37-point pass/fail)\n=================================================================\nA. Methodology: Blended Engine 3+4 justified (transition D\u2192B ~70% met). PASS.\nB. Valuation: DCF/reverse-DCF/multiples triangulate within \u00b115%. PASS.\nC. Bias: Overconfidence audit \u2014 bull case explicitly capped at 20% by base rate; but note: my bear IV ($83) is close to my base ($93) \u2014 the distribution is right-skewed but the mean is pulled by a fat right tail; I checked for herd-bear bias \u2014 the 8% margin-drop reaction could seduce into over-weighting bear. Weight held at 30% on order-backlog evidence. PASS with note.\nD. Consistency: FCF definition (OCF\u2212capex, SBC expensed in NI) applied uniformly from FY26A forward. Q4 FY26 gross margin non-GAAP 66.3% vs 68.4% YoY [Actual] \u2014 properly reflects mix shift. PASS.\nE. Narrative: \"networking supercycle\" translated into explicit revenue/FCF path, sensitivity \u00b1$12/sh. No platform premium without numbers \u2014 AI revenue $7.5B guided, $9.3B orders booked. PASS.\nF. Red Team: executed; logic gap 1.0 \u2192 conviction downgrade applied. PASS.\nG. Data integrity: (1) Pack D&A $0.700B FY25 clearly understated vs Cisco's real depreciation+amortization (confirmed by non-GAAP reconciliation gap of $6.6B FY26) \u2014 I replaced with $2.5B D&A [Assumption] and disclosed. (2) Vendor debt $28.1B vs pack-derived $26.2B \u2014 unresolved, disclosed, sensitivity held. (3) SG&A tag $2.99B is not total opex \u2014 R&D not derivable from pack; labeled [Assumption]. (4) WallStreetZen FY2027 EPS $4.89 conflicts with company guidance $5.08 \u2014 discarded as stale/calendar-mix [Unconfirmed]. PASS.\nAll material flags disclosed. No recalculation required.\n\n=================================================================\nSECTION 11. DECISION JOURNAL ENTRY (v2.0)\n=========================================================